  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Policy Framework and Capacity for Effective Migration and Asylum Management in Armenia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s overarching goal is to strengthen migration governance and enhance refugee protection in Armenia through comprehensive measures. It builds upon recent political reforms and the establishment of the Ministry of Internal Affairs (MIA) and the Migration and Citizenship Service (MCS), focusing on key objectives related to policy development, data management, and asylum procedures.A pivotal aspect of the project is the development of a comprehensive Migration Strategy, which will involve inter-ministerial collaboration, consultations with civil society, and validation workshops to ensure alignment with international standards. Concurrently, upgrading the State Population Register will enhance data collection, sharing, and utilization, while maintaining compatibility with existing e-governance initiatives.To streamline services for foreigners, the project aims to introduce a &quot;one-stop shop&quot; approach, facilitated by legislative amendments and the creation of an online application system. Capacity-building efforts will focus on beneficiary-centered induction training and technical programs for MCS staff, empowering them with the necessary skills and knowledge.Furthermore, the project aims to improve the quality and integrity of asylum procedures by upgrading infrastructure, implementing robust quality assurance mechanisms, and promoting digitalization. It also prioritizes the enhancement of reception facilities for asylum-seekers, ensuring dignified living conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
